commit_sha":"33a43cfa906ebf8bf94371ddfb2c5d5d14cc85a9","position":"1785439063403736001-33f05adc-fc00-4d91-88a6-9157f1cdd679"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0874488d647e722833d3a05fede955be33a2bdd10b6e002807f127de4fcda230","event_uuid":"6d2edc22-b13b-4365-912d-f20ced2ffd37","position":{"commit_sha":"c8bd2b063db8e1897c3fcd4a0e86c27d461eb97a","position":"1785439184139512001-6d2edc22-b13b-4365-912d-f20ced2ffd37"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c313e54c95123978ea5409ae9efc86161e241a5d9fe6f38c015a0e7af94526dd","event_uuid":"7464deab-5edb-4319-b5e5-435c2157e5e3","position":{"commit_sha":"c8bd2b063db8e1897c3fcd4a0e86c27d461eb97a","position":"1785439184685521001-7464deab-5edb-4319-b5e5-435c2157e5e3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"43173d6f85cd0ea2ba417d6c62e41d4bc3b59b8c92f7d24a154c92fc83db6493","event_uuid":"3595aeb8-2206-41b1-b135-6b3ed48ef8c8","position":{"commit_sha":"1e05daa3058901cc586ab1790f4346b1937527c9","position":"1785439363541152001-3595aeb8-2206-41b1-b135-6b3ed48ef8c8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b707f729-f629-4867-9965-f2ea0e303433","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1056 (commit 020038055, Change-Id If8b30699f6d5e1063f0578902a67334b84f712b8).\n\nChange: .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml test-job default-suite step now selects the coverage flags per-OS; docs/coverage.md gained a 'CI collects coverage on the ubuntu cells only' section recording the rationale and the measurements.\n\nImplementation note worth keeping: the flags are selected as\n  ${{ !startsWith(matrix.os, 'macos') && '--cov=rebar --cov-report=term-missing:skip-covered' || '' }}\nNOT the more natural-reading\n  ${{ matrix.os == 'macos-latest' && '' || '--cov=...' }}\nThe second form is a silent no-op: GitHub Actions treats the empty string as FALSY, so 'a && \"\" || b' evaluates to b on BOTH branches and coverage would still have been collected on macOS. Putting the empty branch in the || slot avoids that.\n\nLocal verification (worktree ../ci-macos-nocov, venv on PATH):\n  make lint                                    PASS (ruff check + format, actionlint over all workflows, zizmor, dco/criteria checks)\n  make typecheck                               PASS (mypy, 398 source files)\n  pytest test_ci_workflow_parity.py            6 passed\n  pytest test_workflow_names.py + 3 others     62 passed total\n  scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py          OK (vote.needs covers all 6 gating jobs)\n  yaml.safe_load of the workflow               folds to a single-line command as intended\n\nNot yet verified: the actual macOS speedup. That is observational and this change's own Verified run is the measurement — compare its 'pytest (macos-latest, py3.13)' default-suite step against the 15.4m baseline from run #1823 (id 30569775555), and confirm the pass count is still 7856 and that the ubuntu cells still print a coverage report.","timestamp":1785439363541152001}],"created_at":1785438651200264001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"32667b8f-915b-4fca-98e0-e4eedaae367d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"42eb-5789-c798-4dfc"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe Gerrit Verified gate takes 21-47 minutes end-to-end. Measured on run #1823 (id 30569775555), the critical path is a SINGLE job: `pytest (macos-latest, py3.13)` at 18.6m. Every other job is <=8m; if macOS vanished the run would finish in ~8m.\n\nWorse, macOS runner concurrency is capped (peak 4 concurrent macOS jobs observed across 25 sampled jobs from the last 30 runs). When 6 changes were dispatched within 10 seconds, the later ones queued 6.7-8.4m for a macOS runner. That queue is what turns a 21m run into the 41-47m the operator observes. So macOS job DURATION is doubly valuable: it is both the critical path and the thing holding a scarce runner slot other changes wait on.\n\nWithin that job, the `--cov` default-suite step is 15.4m of the 18.6m. The macOS cells pass `--cov=rebar --cov-report=term-missing:skip-covered`, so coverage.py traces the entire run — but NOTHING consumes the macOS coverage number. The `fail_under = 70` floor in `[tool.coverage.report]` is enforced identically by the three ubuntu cells running the exact same test selection.\n\n## Approach\nMake the coverage flags conditional on the matrix OS in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`: ubuntu cells keep `--cov=rebar --cov-report=term-missing:skip-covered`, macOS cells run without them. This is pure duplicate-work removal — the identical 7856 tests still execute on macOS, and the coverage floor is still gated three times over on ubuntu.\n\nRejected alternative: dropping the macOS cell entirely. That is the obvious 2x win and it removes exactly the platform-compat coverage (flock/mkdir lock, gtimeout) the cell exists for. Out of bounds — the requirement is no coverage loss.\n\nRejected alternative: keep `--cov` on macOS but add `--cov-fail-under=0`. Pointless: it retains the tracing cost, which IS the cost, and only removes an assertion that already passes.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` — the `test` job default-suite step only. The integration-tier step already passes no `--cov` and is untouched. The `-n` worker counts, `--dist` modes, `--basetemp`, and every drift gate are untouched.\n- `docs/coverage.md` — record that coverage is collected on the ubuntu cells only, and why.\n\nExplicitly NOT in scope: sharding the macOS job, changing `-n`, and the verify-identity partial-clone fix (recorded on epic 42eb-5789-c798-4dfc). Those are separate changes with their own risk profiles.\n\n## Testing\nNo new testable behavior — this is a CI workflow configuration change, so no new unit test is warranted. `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` pins the substring `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` (line 67), which this change preserves; that suite must stay green. Verification is observational on the next Verified run: the macOS default-suite step gets faster with an unchanged pass count, and the ubuntu cells still print the coverage report.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The macOS matrix cells run the default suite with no `--cov` or `--cov-report` flags.\n- [ ] The ubuntu matrix cells still pass `--cov=rebar --cov-report=term-missing:skip-covered`.\n- [ ] The `-m \"not integration and not external\"` selection is byte-identical on both platforms, so the set of tests executed on macOS is unchanged.\n- [ ] `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` passes.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] `docs/coverage.md` states that CI collects coverage on the ubuntu cells only.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"make the --cov flags conditional on matrix.os in the test job default-suite step"},{"path":"docs/coverage.md","reason":"record that coverage is collected on the ubuntu cells only"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","42eb-5789-c798-4dfc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6d2edc22-b13b-4365-912d-f20ced2ffd37","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f3d4-c062-31e4-4713","ticket_type":"task","title":"Drop coverage collection from the macOS pytest cells (CI wall-clock)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4c2a3ba3-a6d6-4e30-ace0-7c1977c58293","8792bf5c-c62f-4ea5-8e6d-5189be5fbcf5","32667b8f-915b-4fca-98e0-e4eedaae367d","4063cfab-e1a1-4b8d-9a6c-3b4980a8733d","33f05adc-fc00-4d91-88a6-9157f1cdd679","6d2edc22-b13b-4365-912d-f20ced2ffd37","7464deab-5edb-4319-b5e5-435c2157e5e3","3595aeb8-2206-41b1-b135-6b3ed48ef8c8"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785439363541152002,"uuid":"bfeccb73-e305-4acc-a6c5-3ab2c0aad289"}